! Baseline + soil + crowding, each switchable (AA4)

Both modifications in one model, each behind its own switch.

|!`soil-on?` |!`crowding-on?` |!Model |
|OFF |OFF |[[Baseline]] |
|ON |OFF |[[Soil]] |
|OFF |ON |[[Crowding]] |
|ON |ON |both mechanisms |

The soil and crowding sliders have no effect while their switch is OFF. In the code, `soil-on?` OFF skips the soil update and makes the setup quality draw use `harvest-variance`, as the baseline does. `crowding-on?` OFF makes `crowd-cap`, the effective crowding limit, return 1. With both ON, depletion scales with the number of households working a plot. Both switches default to ON.

